2G, 3G, 4G, LTE, 5G

G = Generation of cellular technology being used

technology                      Frequency                 Speed
1G                              30 KHz                  2 Kbps
2G                              1800 MHz                14.4-64 Kbps
3G                              1.6-2 GHz               144 Kbps - 2 Mbps                   (No need to remember for exam)
4G                              2-8 GHz                 100 Mbps - 1 Gbps
4G LTE (Long Term Evolution)    
5G                         (Low-band) 600-850 MHz       30-250 Mbps
                           (Mid-band) 2.5-3.7 GHz       100-900 Mbps                        
                           (High-band) 25-39 GHz        Extremely fast (in Gbps)


                           (Just remember higher the G the faster and 5G is split into 3 bands)
                           Lowband used for further distance, but lower speeds
                           Midband used for good distance for good speeds 
                           Highband used for short distance, high speeds


Global System for Mobile Communications (GSM) - Cellular tech that takes the voice during a call and then converts it to digital data
Code-Division Multiple Access (CDMA) - Cellulary tech that uses code division to split up the channel

CDMA > GSM

GSM adopted feastures of CDMA -> WCDMA or UMTS

Depends on where you live and service provider

US (T-Mobile/AT&T)      GSM
US (Verizon)            CDMA
Japan/South Korea       CDMA
Other Countries         GSM